<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11213" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornĭ-pēs</span></b> ,
			pĕdis, adj.
		cornu, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>hornfooted, hoofed</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capella,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					19, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 591</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Faunus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					2, 361</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">planta (Panis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					13, 338</span></i>
			.—Also <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornĭpēs</span></b> ,
				pĕdis, m. (so most freq. in
			Claud.), <i>a horn-footed animal;</i> of <i>the horse</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 3,
			361</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 684</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Claud. Fesc. 11, 11 al.</span></i>; of
				<i>the centaur Chiron</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Claud. in Rufin. 2, 180</span></i> et
		saep.</div>
